## 6. What is Context?

Context is like a **global variable** that any component can read without passing props down through every level:

```ts
// Without context — prop drilling hell:
<App user={user}>
  <Dashboard user={user}>
    <TaskList user={user}>
      <TaskCard user={user} />   // passed through 3 levels just to get here
    </TaskList>
  </Dashboard>
</App>

// With context — any component just calls useAuth():
function ProfileScreen() {
  const { cookie, logout } = useAuth(); // grabs it directly, no props needed
}
```

In your app, `AuthContext` holds the session cookie and is available to every screen.

