## 8. What is hardcoded vs real API data

Here's the honest breakdown of your current app:

```
REAL (hits your actual backend)     HARDCODED (fake data)
────────────────────────────────    ──────────────────────────────
✅ Signup → POST /api/auth/signup   ❌ Analytics numbers (24, 14, 6)
✅ Login  → POST /api/auth/login    ❌ Analytics bar percentages
✅ Logout → POST /api/auth/logout   ❌ Settings rows (static list)
✅ Tasks  → GET  /api/tasks         ❌ DUMMY tasks (fallback only)
✅ Mark complete → PATCH /api/tasks/:id/complete
```

The dummy tasks are a **fallback** — if the API call fails, you see dummy data instead of a blank screen. Once your backend `/tasks` endpoint returns real data, the real tasks show automatically.

