## 9. How the cookie auth works end to end

```
SIGNUP                          LOGIN
──────                          ─────
1. Fill form                    1. Enter userName + password
2. POST /api/auth/signup        2. POST /api/auth/login
   body: {                         body: {
     name, userName,                 userName,
     email, phone, password          password
   }                              }
3. Backend creates User         3. Backend checks password (bcrypt)
   in Postgres                  4. Creates session in Redis:
4. Returns:                        key: "app:userId:hashedToken"
   { message: 'User created' }     value: session data
                                5. Returns:
                                   { cookieValue: "userId.token" }
                                6. App saves cookieValue to
                                   AsyncStorage
                                7. Attaches it as Cookie header
                                   on every future request:
                                   Cookie: sessionId=userId.token
```

