## 11. StyleSheet — how styling works

React Native has no CSS. Styles are JavaScript objects:

```ts
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  card: {
    backgroundColor: '#ffffff',
    borderRadius: 12,      // rounded corners
    padding: 16,           // space inside
    marginBottom: 16,      // space outside below
    // shadows (iOS)
    shadowColor: '#000',
    shadowOpacity: 0.1,
    shadowRadius: 8,
    // shadows (Android)
    elevation: 4,
  }
});

// Used like:
<View style={styles.card}>
```

Dynamic styles (based on state or theme) are merged in arrays:
```ts
<View style={[
  styles.input,                           // base style always
  focused && styles.inputFocused,         // added when focused
  error ? styles.inputError : null,       // added when error exists
]} />
```

