## 13. FlatList — the right way to render lists

```ts
// WRONG for long lists — renders ALL items at once, kills performance:
tasks.map(task => <TaskCard task={task} />)

// CORRECT — only renders what's visible on screen:
<FlatList
  data={tasks}              // the array
  keyExtractor={item => item.id}   // unique key for each item
  renderItem={({ item }) => <TaskCard item={item} />}  // how to render each
  numColumns={2}            // for grid layout
/>
```

FlatList is like a smart window — it only renders the items you can actually see, recycling components as you scroll.

