## 14. What to learn next for Android development

In order of importance:

```
1. React hooks deeply          useState, useEffect, useRef, useContext
2. TypeScript basics           interfaces, types, generics
3. React Navigation            stack, tabs, drawer navigators
4. Async/await & fetch         all API calls use this
5. AsyncStorage                local persistence
6. Flexbox layout              how ALL positioning works in RN
7. React Native Reanimated     smooth animations
8. Form handling               validation patterns
9. Error boundaries            graceful crash handling
10. Expo vs bare RN            understand the difference
```

The single most important thing — **understand Flexbox**. Every layout in React Native is Flexbox. No floats, no grid (CSS grid), no absolute positioning by default. Just `flexDirection`, `justifyContent`, and `alignItems`.

```ts
// This centers anything:
<View style={{ flex: 1, justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center' }}>
  <Text>I am perfectly centered</Text>
</View>
```

