## 15. The complete request lifecycle in your app

When you tap "Create account":

```
1. Button onPress fires
2. validate() runs — checks all fields locally
3. If valid → setLoading(true) → spinner shows on button
4. fetch() sends HTTP POST to 10.0.2.2:8000/api/auth/signup
5. Request travels: Emulator → PC network → Express server
6. Express → validateZod middleware runs your Zod schema
7. If valid → registerClient() called → bcrypt hashes password
8. Sequelize INSERT into Postgres Users table
9. Response comes back: { message: 'User created successfully' }
10. App shows Alert → navigates to Login
11. setLoading(false) → button returns to normal
```

If anything in steps 5-9 fails, the catch block runs and shows an error alert. That's the complete picture.


